    "Claims profile for scripts/check_copy.py: US dietary supplements, built on amazon-standard.",
    "Free text keys stay at label facts and neutral routine or format wording. Disease, body-system and effect words are errors there; an approved structure/function line goes only in a key the skeleton lists in sf_keys, which the gate checks against approved_sf_lines instead of this list.",
    "Quality, testing, certification, origin and free-from words are errors unless the product's facts file lifts the exact pattern with allow, backed by evidence a human has approved.",
    "Use and format words beyond the label's suggested use (timing, with food, capsule size) are errors until the label or an approved source says so.",
    "disclaimer: every frame that holds an S/F line must carry a key named key whose text starts with prefix; name is the word used in the error.",
    "Patterns run on the normalized text and ignore case. See amazon-standard.json for the merge rules."
